{%- comment -%}
  HLT One — first-order signup, rebuilt around the 20% offer.

  Paste this into the "Custom Liquid" field of the existing section in Theme
  Editor. It replaces the markup only; the section wrapper, colour scheme and
  padding settings stay as they are.

  ── HOW IT SUBMITS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  This uses Shopify's native customer form, so the address lands in Customers
  with marketing consent recorded, and syncs through to Klaviyo on the existing
  integration. If the current block posts straight to Klaviyo instead, keep that
  mechanism and lift only the visual layer out of here: swapping the transport
  as well is how addresses go missing quietly.

  ── THE CODE STILL HAS TO BE SENT ────────────────────────────────────────────
  A form that captures the address does not deliver anything. The 20% code needs
  a Klaviyo flow triggered on the subscribe event, and a matching discount in
  Shopify. Without both, this promises something the customer never receives.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .hlt-join {
    --navy: #1b2e5c;
    --navy-deep: #14224a;
    --cream: #fffbf1;
    --sky: #6cb4e4;
    --ink-soft: #55637f;
    --line: rgba(27, 46, 92, .14);
    --font: inherit;

    /* ---- Type sizes. Everything adjustable lives here. ----
       Deliberately px, not rem. A rem is a share of the theme's root size, and
       plenty of Shopify themes set that root to 62.5%, which quietly turns
       1.2rem into 12px instead of 19px. px renders the same number whatever the
       theme did upstream.

       The cost of that choice: px ignores a reader who has raised their browser
       font size. If that matters more than predictability here, swap these back
       to rem and check the rendered pixel value in DevTools before trusting it.

       The title is a clamp: first value is the floor on a phone, last is the
       ceiling on a desktop, middle scales between. Move the first and last
       together or the two ends drift apart. */
    --fs-badge: 14px;
    --fs-title: clamp(34px, 5vw, 52px);
    --fs-sub: 19px;
    --fs-field: 17px;
    --fs-consent: 15px;

    /* ---- Widths ----
       The block gets wider, but the prose does not follow it all the way. A
       line of body copy running the full 1200px would be past 120 characters,
       which is roughly double what the eye tracks comfortably; the reader loses
       their place on the return sweep. So the shell widens and the paragraphs
       stay capped by character count instead. */
    --max-w: 1200px;
    --measure-sub: 62ch;
    --measure-consent: 66ch;
    --w-form: 620px;

    max-width: var(--max-w);
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
    /* The section this sits in has lost its padding sliders, so the breathing
       room is carried here instead. If those sliders ever come back, drop this
       line rather than running both and doubling the gap. */
    padding: clamp(56px, 7vw, 88px) 20px;
  }

  /* The offer leads. The old version opened on brand language and left the
     reader to work out what they were being asked for. */
  .hlt-join__badge {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--sky);
    color: var(--navy);
    font-size: var(--fs-badge);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 8px 18px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
  }

  .hlt-join__title {
    color: var(--navy);
    font-size: var(--fs-title);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -.01em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hlt-join__title em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sky); }

  .hlt-join__sub {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-sub);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0 auto 32px;
    max-width: var(--measure-sub);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .hlt-join__form { display: block; }

  .hlt-join__row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    max-width: var(--w-form);
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .hlt-join__input {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    min-width: 0;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--fs-field);
    color: var(--navy);
    background: #fff;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 17px 24px;
    transition: border-color .2s ease, box-shadow .2s ease;
  }

  .hlt-join__input::placeholder { color: #93a0b8; }

  .hlt-join__input:focus {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--navy);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(27, 46, 92, .12);
  }

  /* Navy rather than the sky blue of the old button. White on that light blue
     came out around 2.4:1, which is below the 4.5:1 needed for body-size text
     and reads as washed out on any screen in daylight. Navy clears 11:1. */
  .hlt-join__btn {
    flex: none;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--fs-field);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .01em;
    color: #fff;
    background: var(--navy);
    border: none;
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 17px 32px;
    cursor: pointer;
    white-space: nowrap;
    transition: background-color .2s ease, transform .15s ease, box-shadow .2s ease;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(27, 46, 92, .2);
  }

  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .hlt-join__btn:hover {
      background: var(--navy-deep);
      transform: translateY(-1px);
      box-shadow: 0 12px 26px rgba(27, 46, 92, .26);
    }
  }

  .hlt-join__btn:active { transform: scale(.98); }

  .hlt-join__btn:focus-visible {
    outline: 2.5px solid var(--navy);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Consent has to be visible at the point of submission, not buried in a
     policy page, and it is what makes these addresses safe to put in a
     marketing flow. */
  .hlt-join__consent {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-consent);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin: 18px auto 0;
    max-width: var(--measure-consent);
  }

  .hlt-join__consent a { color: var(--ink-soft); text-decoration: underline; }

  .hlt-join__note {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--fs-consent);
    margin: 8px 0 0;
  }

  .hlt-join__msg {
    max-width: var(--w-form);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    font-size: var(--fs-field);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .hlt-join__msg--ok {
    background: #eaf5ec;
    border: 1px solid #bfe0c6;
    color: #1d5b2c;
  }

  .hlt-join__msg--err {
    background: #fdeceb;
    border: 1px solid #f3c2be;
    color: #9a2b22;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 620px) {
    .hlt-join__row { flex-direction: column; }
    .hlt-join__btn { width: 100%; padding: 17px 26px; }
    .hlt-join__sub { font-size: 17px; }
  }
</style>

<div class="hlt-join">

  <span class="hlt-join__badge">First order</span>

  <h2 class="hlt-join__title">Take <em>20% off</em> your first order</h2>

  <p class="hlt-join__sub">
    Join the HLT One family for members-only bundles, first look at new arrivals,
    and rewards every time you shop.
  </p>

  {%- form 'customer', class: 'hlt-join__form' -%}
    {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}

      <p class="hlt-join__msg hlt-join__msg--ok">
        You're in. Your 20% code is on its way to your inbox, so keep an eye on
        it (and the promotions tab).
      </p>

    {%- else -%}

      <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter,first-order-20">
      {%- comment -%}
        Shopify records marketing consent from this field, which is what makes
        these profiles eligible for a marketing flow rather than transactional
        mail only.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <input type="hidden" name="contact[accepts_marketing]" value="true">

      <div class="hlt-join__row">
        <label class="visually-hidden" for="hlt-join-email">Email address</label>
        <input
          id="hlt-join-email"
          class="hlt-join__input"
          type="email"
          name="contact[email]"
          value="{{ form.email }}"
          placeholder="Your email address"
          autocomplete="email"
          autocorrect="off"
          autocapitalize="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          required
        >
        <button type="submit" class="hlt-join__btn">Unlock 20% off</button>
      </div>

      {%- if form.errors -%}
        <p class="hlt-join__msg hlt-join__msg--err" style="margin-top:14px;">
          {{ form.errors.messages.email | default: "That address didn't look right. Mind checking it?" }}
        </p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <p class="hlt-join__consent">
        By joining you agree to receive marketing emails from HLT One. One code
        per customer, valid on your first order. Unsubscribe any time.
      </p>

    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endform -%}

</div>
